.TH ZSTD-SPLITTER 1 "July 2026" "zstd-splitter 4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zstd-splitter \- create, split, verify, transfer, reconstruct and extract compressed tar archives
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zstd-splitter -c -s size [options] source
.br
.B zstd-splitter -j [options] part
.br
.B zstd-splitter -x [options] input
.br
.B zstd-splitter -v [options] input
.br
.B zstd-splitter -P -i -R destination [options] input
.br
.B zstd-splitter -G -i -R remote-input [options]
.br
.B zstd-splitter -Q mode [ -R destination ] [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Version 4.0 is a POSIX /bin/sh utility for selectable tar compression engines, deterministic split-part naming, optional strict SHA-256 manifests, and version-gated SSH/SFTP workflows.
.PP
Strict mode records a canonical source inventory, the compressed archive size and SHA-256, and the size and SHA-256 of every part. Verification and extraction recheck the applicable layers before publication.
.SH LOCAL ACTIONS
.TP
.B -c
Create, compress and split a tar stream.
.TP
.B -j
Verify and join split parts.
.TP
.B -x
Extract an archive or a verified part set.
.TP
.B -v
Verify without extraction.
.TP
.B -E
List compression engines.
.SH NETWORK ACTIONS
.TP
.B -P
Push one local archive or strict part set.
.TP
.B -G
Pull one remote archive or part set.
.TP
.BI -Q " mode"
Run one of: network, config.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BI -e " engine"
Select zstd, gzip, bzip2, xz, lzma, lzip, lzop or lz4.
.TP
.BI -s " size"
Maximum split-part size.
.TP
.BI -l " level"
Codec-specific compression level.
.TP
.BI -T " threads"
Worker count for supported codecs.
.TP
.B -i
Enable strict integrity.
.TP
.BI -m " manifest"
Use an explicit strict manifest.
.TP
.BI -d " directory"
Extraction or pull destination.
.TP
.B -f
Allow replacement; also required for destructive GC in 4.2 releases.
.TP
.BI -R " [user@]host:/absolute/path"
Select a remote source or destination.
.TP
.BI -O " name=value"
Set one network option; repeatable.
.TP
.BI -F " file"
Read network options from a file.
.SH NETWORK MODEL
All 4.x releases provide strict single-destination push/pull, retry, staging, locking, remote verification, atomic bundle publication, optional remote extraction, bandwidth limiting, bastion/identity controls, and safe host-key policies.

.SS 4.1 boundary
Profiles, parallel workers, SFTP-window tuning, connection-reuse tuning, and route/MTU diagnostics are rejected by this release.
.SS 4.2 administration boundary
Fan-out, quorum, relay, health, inventory, garbage collection and JSONL audit are rejected.

.SH PORTABILITY
This original feature release expects the GNU-oriented dependency set documented in the package. Use the corresponding .1 maintenance release for macOS/BSD abstraction.
.SH FEATURE LEVEL
The executable declares FEATURE_LEVEL=40. Dormant later-version helper functions in the shared source are not public capabilities; runtime gates and tests enforce this boundary.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I *.manifest.sha256
Strict integrity manifest.
.TP
.I *.part.aaaaaa
Split archive part.
.TP
.I *.bundle
Atomically published remote bundle directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 for success, 1 for operational or integrity failure, and 2 for invalid syntax, invalid options, or a feature-gate violation.
.SH SECURITY
StrictHostKeyChecking is never disabled. Remote payload files remain partial until verified. Manifests are parsed as data and are not sourced as shell code.

.SH RUNTIME SECURITY AUDIT
The 2026-07-28 package revision uses a private umask, sanitized command
lookup, private temporary directories, global signal cleanup, receiver-side
verification, transactional local and remote publication, and explicit
cleanup of remote staging and persistent SSH control masters.
Archive members are listed and checked before extraction into a private
staging tree. FIFO, device, socket, control-character path, ambiguous
manifest, option-like SSH target, and unsafe jump-hop inputs are refused.
.PP
The environment variable
.B ZSTD_SPLITTER_TMPDIR
is the only supported override for the private network temporary parent;
ambient
.B TMPDIR
is intentionally ignored. The override and every directory in
.B ZSTD_SPLITTER_PATH
must be administrator-controlled.
.PP
SHA-256 manifests provide integrity but not origin authentication. Running
untrusted extraction as root, operating in attacker-writable parent
directories, resource exhaustion, and concurrent source mutation remain
outside the protection that a portable shell script can fully guarantee.
See
.B docs/RUNTIME-SECURITY.md
in the distribution.

.SH SEE ALSO
tar(1), ssh(1), sftp(1), sha256sum(1), shasum(1), openssl(1)
